        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): account-scoped voice groups + delayed autoJoin safety net",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw can run multiple Discord bot accounts in one guild, but `@discordjs/voice` stores connections by `(group, guildId)` and defaults every caller to the same `default` group. One account can therefore reuse or destroy another account's voice connection. Auto-join can also miss startup when the Discord gateway is already READY before the voice listener is registered.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe connection owner now supplies a stable `openclaw:<accountId>` group for lookup, join, and cleanup. Provider startup also checks the existing gateway readiness state immediately after registering READY/RESUMED listeners. This closes the ordering race directly and removes the earlier 6-, 8-, and 75-second timing workarounds.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDiscord accounts sharing a guild keep independent voice connections. Configured voice auto-join starts whether readiness happened just before listener registration or arrives later through READY/RESUMED. No configuration or command changes are required.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Direct `@discordjs/voice` 0.19.2 source inspection confirmed its process-global registry is keyed by guild plus caller-provided group and defaults to `default`.\n- Focused Blacksmith Testbox run passed 165 Discord voice/provider tests, including two account managers targeting the same guild and an already-ready gateway: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28749942082\n- Changed-surface gate passed: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28749991095\n- Fresh Codex autoreview found no actionable issues.\n- The current maintainer host has no configured multi-account Discord voice setup, so live two-account proof is unavailable; the regression tests exercise the dependency's exact registry and lifecycle contracts.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Scope every voice connection operation by account ID.\n- Start auto-join synchronously when the lifecycle gateway is already connected.\n- Preserve READY and RESUMED listeners for later reconnects.\n- Remove all timer-based startup retries.\n",
